<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lewiston, New York</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lewiston is a town in Niagara County, in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niagara-river">Niagara River</a> below the falls and across from Queenston, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>. The reservation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-people">Tuscarora Nation</a>, which settled among the Seneca after migrating north from North Carolina in the 18th century, lies within the town. Lewiston was burned by British forces and their Native allies in December 1813 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lewiston-new-york.jpg" alt="Lewiston, New York" width="320" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rcsprinter123 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niagara_County_New_York_incorporated_and_unincorporated_areas_Lewiston_(town)_highlighted.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
